"""Build the narrow climate integration handoff from common outputs and annual accounts."""
import importlib.util,json
from pathlib import Path
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[2]
s=importlib.util.spec_from_file_location('climate',R/'index/tools/climate-integration.py');C=importlib.util.module_from_spec(s);s.loader.exec_module(C)
f=json.loads((R/'build/fiscal-model.json').read_text());r=json.loads((R/'build/recovery-budget.json').read_text());i=json.loads((R/'build/incidence.json').read_text());b=C.CONFIG['before'];d=f['results']['DEC'];q=next(v for k,v in i.items() if k.startswith('Q.'));rs=r['cases']['mixed_reserve_corridor']['summary']
metrics=[('DEC FY2040 GF primary gap ($B)',b['dec_2040_gf_bn'],d['years']['2040']['gf_primary'],1),('DEC FY2040 GF primary gap (% GDP)',b['dec_2040_gf_pct'],d['years']['2040']['gf_primary_pct'],3),('Recovery mature GF gap (% GDP; negative is headroom)',b['recovery_mature_gap_pct'],rs['max_mature_agenda_gf_gap_gdp'],4),('DEC 2056 debt (% GDP)',b['dec_2056_debt_pct'],d['years']['2056']['debt_pct'],1),('Mixed reserve-corridor 2056 debt (% GDP)',b['recovery_2056_debt_pct'],rs['debt_gdp_2056'],1),('Scenario Q, Q4 annual average ($)',b['q4_average_dollars'],q['res']['Q4']['net'],0),('Mixed recovery Q4 FY2039 ($)',b['mixed_q4_2039_dollars'],r['household_diagnostic']['per_household_annual_dollars']['mixed']['2039']['Q4'],0)]
lines=['# Decided climate package: ledger and recovery integration','', 'Package A, O5 and CLI-7C are integrated using the **conservative** case: central costs and only the low end of credit savings. O5 keeps this climate increment at or below zero for the general fund in FY2040 and FY2050 in all four cases. It does not eliminate the pre-existing DEC gap, finance early costs, or secure D3.','',f"Before: common outputs rebuilt at `{b['source_commit']}`. After: this branch’s common outputs, generated by `index/tools/run-all.sh --write`. This report is generated by `climate-integration-report.py`.",'','| Measure | Before | After |','| --- | ---: | ---: |']
for label,old,new,n in metrics:lines.append(f'| {label} | {old:,.{n}f} | {new:,.{n}f} |')
lines+=['','The mature-year climate delta is zero in the conservative case, so both maturity measures stay unchanged. Debt rises because early general-fund and capital costs are borrowed, with interest. D4 is not relaxed: DEC still fails maturity; the mixed recovery illustration retains only narrow GF headroom and does not certify all-fund solvency. The mixed recovery tax rates remain illustrative.','', '| Climate case | GF 2030–39 $B | D4-B capital $B | GF 2040 $B | GF 2050 $B |','| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |']
for case in C.DATA['budget']['cases']:
 a=C.account(2040,case);z=C.account(2050,case)
 if max(a['general_fund_net_cost_bn'],z['general_fund_net_cost_bn'])>1e-8:raise ValueError('O5 maturity failure: '+case)
 lines.append(f"| {case} | {sum(C.account(y,case)['general_fund_net_cost_bn'] for y in range(2030,2040)):.1f} | {C.capital_tn(case)*1000:.1f} | {a['general_fund_net_cost_bn']:.1f} | {z['general_fund_net_cost_bn']:.1f} |")
lines+=['','## Accounting choices','', '- **Credit split:** the pricing denominator includes $0.90T of CLI-1 and $0.22T of CLI-5 ITC/45X. Allocate the same $178.5B conservative saving proportionally: $143.4B and $35.1B. CLI-1 is consequently $0.757T, not the unreconciled ~$0.72T sketch; CLI-5 gross spending is $0.565T. No second overlap saving is taken. A provision-level joint score remains necessary.', '- **Program rows:** CLI-5W is $67.5B in 2025 dollars over 2031–39 ($84.0B nominal); CLI-10G is the lean grid expected deficit cost ($39.4B), not loan principal. CLI-9 is $109.5B, CLI-13F forests $24.6B and CLI-13A farms $30.8B. CLI-7 permanent disaster pieces, CLI-7N NFIP resolution and CLI-7K capital are disjoint. Standards have zero direct outlay; clean heat starts in 2032.', '- **Receipts and O5:** C1P separately books $244.3B process receipts; CB1 books the $141.6B reduction in combustion receipts. CXP is the 25% net excise offset ($25.7B cost), on top of unchanged baseline CX. CLI-2 includes the incremental dividend; CLI-2O records incremental receipts minus that dividend as financing of gross program rows. The accounting identity is gross GF items + CX + channel uses + dividend − added receipts = net GF cost. D4-B capital is added once, separately. The baseline 20% share remains credited once to CLI-5; none of the $150 step is reused.', '- **Reinsurance:** CLI-7C scores expected net cost, $0.3B per year in 2025 dollars from FY2031 (range −0.3 to +1.0), $3.36B nominal through 2039. The $75–150B contingent exposure appears in D4 records but is not an additional expected outlay. Tail losses and recoupment incidence remain risks.', '- **Capital:** C44 classifies $151.9B of already-booked capital as D4-B borrowing; it is not a saving or an expansion of the envelope. The recovery surge reduction previously freed about $195B: do not credit that saving again. Central/conservative capital uses about $152B, leaving about $43B of that increment; unfavorable capital about $212B exceeds it. DEC retains the historical larger surge and fails maturity, so its capital classification is not a declaration of available borrowing authority.', '- **Long term:** the export ends in 2050. For 2051–56, hold each 2050 real flow constant at the export’s 2.2% inflation rate; ended programs stay ended. This homogeneous extension preserves the O5 identities but is not a new emissions/revenue forecast. No post-2050 fiscal gain from faster abatement is assumed.', '', '## Household limits and next assignment', '', 'The household diagnostic includes the process fee with a full-pass-through consumption proxy, lost combustion fees with the energy key, the actual annual O5 dividend, reduced household credits, and retrofit/bill support with the low-income-energy key. Retrofit spending is an in-kind benefit proxy, not cash. Disaster risk reduction, industrial spillovers, additional system-price effects, within-quintile variation and tail recoupment are not established by these averages. Scenario Q is a ten-year average; the mixed result is FY2039 and uses different financing. Neither establishes D3.','', '**Next bounded scope:** a joint revenue settlement and fourth-quintile protection comparison, owned by the common fiscal integrator. Reconcile G1/G5/G7 and corporate C38 against current law; then price two or three worker/nonworker refundable protection schedules against those net receipts. Test annual household cells (including disability, retirement and self-employment), early affordability, D4 maturity and downside debt without spending the same revenue twice. Return one comparison PR with explicit unresolved ranges; reserve any strategic downsizing decision for Espen. Do not open new program expansions in that task.','', '## Sources and validation','', '- [October 27 governing decisions](../governing/project-2050-governing-decisions.md), [allocation section 5](climate-portfolio-allocation.md), [handoff sections 2–4](codex-handoff-climate-financing-2026-10-26.md).','- [Annual pricing export](climate-portfolio-pricing.json), hash pinned in [climate-adoption.json](../index/data/inputs/climate-adoption.json); export and baseline carbon configuration unchanged. International results and removal purchases excluded.','- [Ledger](../index/2029-trifecta-master-ledger.md), [long-term tests](../index/fiscal-long-term-model.md), [recovery budget](../index/recovery-budget.md), [household diagnostics](../index/revenue-household-incidence-model.md).','- `test_climate_integration.py` checks annual aggregate/component reconciliation, unchanged 80/20 arithmetic, CX, diversion bounds, all four maturity cases, capital end dates, ledger totals and unscored contingency. Full validation results are recorded in the PR.','']
(R/'build/climate-ledger-integration.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines))
